{
 "id": "lem-weil-pbc-projective-embedding",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Projective embedding over the source",
 "statement": "With the notation of [lemma-weil-pbc-chow-factorization], the map\n\n$$\n i_X=(\\pi,i_Y):\\widetilde X\\longrightarrow\n X\\times_Y\\mathbf P^n_Y\\simeq\\mathbf P^n_X\n$$\n\nis a closed immersion over $X$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-reduction/lem-weil-pbc-projective-embedding.md",
  "place": "node lem-weil-pbc-projective-embedding, order 1197"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "lemma-weil-pbc-chow-factorization",
  "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The map $i_X$ is an immersion by the graph construction applied to the two\nmaps supplied by [lemma-weil-pbc-chow-factorization]. Its source is proper over $X$ and its\ntarget is separated over $X$, so $i_X$ is proper; a proper immersion is a\nclosed immersion.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-weil-pbc-chow-factorization"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
